speechtext:
To make the matter a little clearer may I read the subclause we are studying at the moment. It reads as follows:
(i) facilities should be provided within the Canadian broadcasting system for educational broadcasting;
That is the subclause under study at the present time.

Order, please. The hon. member is now speaking of educational programs supplied by the province. The clause now under discussion states:
-facilities should be provided within the Canadian broadcasting system for educational broadcasting;
This does not means, in the opinion of the Chair, that the federal government will interfere in educational programs. The educational programs mentioned by the member are provincial educational programs and are not in the least related to the clause now under consideration.
